RNNoise v0.1.1 ("last classic version", https://github.com/xiph/rnnoise tag v0.1.1,
commit of the tag), BSD-3-Clause (see COPYING), built into the kernel for the
noise-reduced input device ("Internal Microphone (Noise Reduction)") of VoodooHDASofEngine.

Kernel changes (output verified bit-identical to the stock library on a DMIC recording):
  - no libc/libm: rnn_kern.h provides sqrt/fabs (SSE), floor, log10 (atanh series),
    sin/cos (Taylor; only for the one-time FFT twiddles / window / DCT tables);
    FFT state comes from a static arena (rnnk_alloc), nothing is freed
  - 16 KB kernel stack: all large locals and the VLAs in pitch.c / celt_lpc.c are
    static (single instance, the caller serializes); deepest call chain ~2 KB
  - GRU states inline in DenoiseState instead of calloc; rnnoise_create/destroy,
    rnn_reader.c (FILE model loading), the TRAINING main() and stdio removed
  - band gains can be floored (rnnk_gain_floor, the "strength" slider: floor
    10^(-0.02 * %), 100 % = 0 = stock behaviour); applied after the gain smoothing
  - wrapper API: rnnoise_kern.h (rnnk_init / rnnk_set_floor / rnnk_reset / rnnk_process)
